00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.019
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:56.150
Step 1.

00:07:56.499 --> 00:07:59.660
Confirm Business Operations access and configure billing

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.419
identity and approved rates.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:02.640
Step 2.

00:08:02.989 --> 00:08:06.890
Prepare a demo bid or contract and the corresponding service invoice.

00:08:07.329 --> 00:08:08.060
Step 3.

00:08:08.479 --> 00:08:12.360
Review payments, invoice aging, deployment costs, or MARS

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.960
claim evidence as applicable.

00:08:14.579 --> 00:08:16.079
Now verify the result.

00:08:16.479 --> 00:08:20.519
Reconcile source activity, quantities, rates, totals, and

00:08:20.519 --> 00:08:22.499
recorded payment or claim outcomes.

00:08:22.879 --> 00:08:24.890
Use a payment-provider test environment.

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:29.480
A common problem to watch for: Pay-data reporting also requires

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.500
enabled Advanced Data Protection.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:35.550
Annual rates and reporting requirements need current finance review.

00:08:36.229 --> 00:08:37.859
Your practice task is simple.

00:08:38.299 --> 00:08:42.129
Prepare a standby estimate and draft invoice from sample activity.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:46.550
Compare recorded cost with the billed amount and explain any difference.

00:08:46.929 --> 00:08:50.849
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

